meta {
  name: dev link (bob joins this account)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{auth_url}}/oauth/dev/link
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "user": "bob"
  }
}

docs {
  Run "dev token" first. Links the dev-bob identity to the CURRENT
  token's account: expect 200 with linked_provider "dev" and a fresh
  token pair for the same user (the env keeps the original pair; both
  stay valid). After this, logging in as bob lands in this account.

  Re-running is an idempotent 200 (same account). If dev-bob already
  belongs to a DIFFERENT account (someone logged in as bob before ever
  linking), expect 409 identity_already_linked instead: linking never
  moves a login between accounts. Run "unlink identity (bob leaves)"
  to restore the single-login state.
}
